<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Full results for all 12 configurations across three experiment groups. Group A: loss ablation (30 epochs, lr <math id="A1.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>). Group B: loss weight tuning (30 epochs, lr <math id="A1.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}=0</annotation></semantics></math>). Group C: training recipe variations. Baseline: Recall@10 = 0.637, MRR@10 = 0.329.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hidden State Extraction.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The LLM generates queries via greedy decoding with a maximum of 32 new tokens. At each autoregressive step, we extract the last-layer hidden state (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}=4096" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4096</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}=4096</annotation></semantics></math>) and retain only non-special tokens (excluding BOS, EOS, and padding). KV caching is used for efficient generation. All hidden states are stored as float32.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Trace Caching.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To enable rapid experimentation, we cache the LLM’s generation traces (hidden states, query text, token counts) as per-trigger <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.npz</span> files, keyed by a hash of the model name, tokenizer max length, and generation length. A total of 11,017 traces are cached. On cache hit, the LLM is not loaded at all, reducing experiment time from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>2 hours to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>15–20 minutes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Projection Head.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The transformer encoder uses pre-norm layer normalization, 8 attention heads, and a feedforward dimension of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times d_{m}=4096" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4096</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times d_{m}=4096</annotation></semantics></math>. Dropout is set to 0. Learnable positional embeddings (initialized to zeros) support sequences up to 128 tokens. The output projection maps from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}=1024</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1024</annotation></semantics></math> (the embedding model’s output dimension), followed by L2 normalization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use AdamW with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, and gradient clipping at norm 1.0. The learning rate follows a cosine schedule from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> over 80 epochs. Batch size is 16. For rank distillation, the top-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=128</annotation></semantics></math> documents are retrieved per query using the teacher’s embeddings, and their similarity scores serve as the soft targets.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Bootstrap confidence intervals use 1,000 resamples with replacement at the trigger level. McNemar’s test compares per-trigger binary retrieval success (whether the relevant document appears in the top-10 results) between our method and the baseline. All experiments run on a single NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 (Blackwell architecture, 98GB VRAM).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
